{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1293552-mixing-era-splats","id":1293552,"title":"Mixing Era splats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-03T15:42:11-08:00","id":1293552,"title":"Mixing Era splats","content":"So I\u2019m wondering is there anything wrong with fully mixing splat rules when we have Aberrant and Adventure, as well as others like Anima and Aegis?<br /> <br /> Like we know Adventure has simplified rules, just calling things Telluric energies. But could say Bhurano have some Mesmerist Knacks? Wouldn\u2019t she be hella more potent then the other Proxies with her two centuries of experience even without the variety of powers from adding knacks?<br /> <br /> But what about evolving splats by say starting as a Stalwart and becoming more like a Nova in Play?<br /> <br /> And in general using say Aeon Psi user rules for an Aberrant game, like they having one off Psions, maybe in a mixed Talent Nova Group.<br /> <br /> Or a Nova in a Psion group in the Aeon setting.<br /> <br /> I mean it sounds intentional to me to cover all these Eras with a caveat that you can cannibalize the rules to make such splats in other Eras.<br /> <br /> I know the number of Psi and Quantum users effect each other but so we have a rough population count for all three Inspired in Adventure, Nova Age and Aeon Age? Like how many Novas did they have at the peak? Were Talents effected by the others rise in Numbers?<br /> <br /> People have told me the contrary, advocating for not mixing timeline rules, and using each Corebook as a separate game, but I feel this is a unified shared timeline so it should be fine to mix and match if you have a solid theme you have planned for you game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T17:03:22-08:00","id":1293580,"title":"","content":"To my mind, mixing Era splats is best done either in A) a time travel story, or B) deep space.<br /> <br /> For the first, allow an Inspired inventor to build a time machine that goes REAL bad. And pull a group of inspired, Novas, talents, and Psions to a city on Ancient Earth which seems to fit the requirements of Atlantis, or does it. Hidden secret? Alien plot? Alternate universe?<br /> <br /> For the second, try a world settled by a Nova fleeing the Aberrant wars with a group of humans, Psiads, and weaker Novas in tow. He Taints out through massive power overuse and throws the others to safety through a warp before he explodes (his Taint expressed itself that way). The Warp was unstable and the group is lost in time and space. They land on a viable world with the supplies they need to survive. The humans (of all splats) cause the extinction of the local lifeforms, but not until they've replaced them. Thousands of years later the star wandering is the sacred beginning tale. In a world of Talents, Inspired, Psions/Psiads, and Low Level Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-04-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T17:31:02-08:00","id":1293587,"title":"","content":"One particular story idea I like is a group of humans from various time Periods, so retired Gladiator, depression era actress, 1st gen mars colonist, etc. They are kept in a black market alien Zoo, and then they escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> But besides that it\u2019s relatively easy to have one or two members in a group from another time period, like Adventure Era Stalwart Frozen in Ice after stopping a Nazi Rocket Being unfrozen and joining a group of Aeon Era Psions, along with the talent members of one of the Psion Groups, and Maybe a human who survived an experimental rocket and turned into some sort of Nova Warper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In fact we don\u2019t have a generic name for the groups do we? Like Stalwarts aren\u2019t a type of Nova, and Superiors are also different. Novas are specifically those who erupt from the ambient Quantum from Mal\u2019s experiment, or the children of such beings right? But would someone bitten by a Radioactive Spider or uplifted from an Alien Battery be Novas or would we need another word?<br /> <br /> How are Daredevils different from Inspired, the impression I get is in 2nd ed the Inspired and Daredevils are the same beings, with maybe a local fad in certain expressions of inspired power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T17:35:59-08:00","id":1293588,"title":"","content":"Also with Preabberant Mutants, are they just lowest level Quantum, high corruption Novas? Are they mostly limited to powers derived from physical mutations? Are they comparable to Stalwarts but highly mutated? They seem similar to say Fomori from Werewolf. Can SubAberrant Mutants evolve into Novas or Stalwarts? Are they actually weaker to Stalwarts?<br /> <br /> The biggest difference now I know between them and Novas besides power is they can be reliably created right? The trade off is corruption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:24:05-08:00","id":1293602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact we don\u2019t have a generic name for the groups do we? Like Stalwarts aren\u2019t a type of Nova, and Superiors are also different. Novas are specifically those who erupt from the ambient Quantum from Mal\u2019s experiment, or the children of such beings right? But would someone bitten by a Radioactive Spider or uplifted from an Alien Battery be Novas or would we need another word?<br /> <br /> How are Daredevils different from Inspired, the impression I get is in 2nd ed the Inspired and Daredevils are the same beings, with maybe a local fad in certain expressions of inspired power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was what Eximorph (Nova, Stalwarts, Superiors, Aberrants), Psychomorph (Psions, Psaids, Mesmercists) and Paramorph (Talents, Daredevil*) terms were for.<br /> <br /> And I remember asking during the kickstarter, but I think that offically Talents are just another more modern name for Daredevils now.<br /> <br /> Certainly that is what Ian Watson said <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1073186#post1073186\">here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:26:58-08:00","id":1293604,"title":"","content":"Doh yeah forgot about those Morph words! Thanks for the reminder!<br /> <br /> Alright so officially Daredevils are interchangeable with Talents good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T19:17:16-08:00","id":1293624,"title":"","content":"If it also helps, I think in 1st edition, Subaberrants weren't eximorphs and this couldn't become a Nova or a Stalwart. They were neutrals/baselines mutated by an Aberrant. The trade off was a lack of power and advancement compared to actual Aberrants. Additional, they were formed from Corruption/Taint (still true in 2e) so that is considered a feature rather than a flaw.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, I would argue this makes Talents and psychomorphs resistant if not immune to the transformative effects of Coruption. Probably give them some sort of cancer instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T05:44:19-08:00","id":1293712,"title":"","content":"I don't see how that would be a problem. They all use the same rules after all. I think intercompatibility was one of the design goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:17:08-08:00","id":1293722,"title":"","content":"It would be like writing for the Justice League, Batman (a talent), Superman, Martian Manhunter, Flash, Black Canary, Green Lantern, Firestorm, (Novas) Hawkgirl, Atom, (Stalwarts), Zatanna (Mage), Aquaman and Wonder Woman (Scions), all need roles in the story. So you need to make sure they have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-04-2019, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:38:25-08:00","id":1293772,